      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.648,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Working with Fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.41,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "Once again, we have —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.108,
            0.462,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered $= { \\frac { 2 } { 5 } } \\times 3$ km."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.144,
            0.798,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.304,
            0.373,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "**Finding the product:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.337,
            0.677,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": "1. We can first find the distance covered in $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ hours."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.372,
            0.847,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "2. Since, the duration $\\frac{2}{5}$ is twice ${ \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } ,$ we multiply this distance by 2 to get the total distance covered."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.429,
            0.385,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "Here is the calculation."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.453,
            0.498,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour = 3 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.481,
            0.462,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "1. Distance covered in $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ hour"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.52,
            0.714,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "= The length we get by dividing 3 km in 5 equal parts $= \\frac{3}{5}$ km."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.583,
            0.562,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": "2. Multiplying this distance by 2, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.614,
            0.582,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "2 \\times \\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{6}{5}    km .",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.646,
            0.412,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "From this we can see that"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.677,
            0.545,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { 2 } { 5 } } \\times 3 = { \\frac { 6 } { 5 } } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.728,
            0.29,
            0.749
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Discussion"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.759,
            0.523,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": "We did this multiplication as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.784,
            0.437,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "• First, we divided the multiplicand, 3 , by the"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.732,
            0.859,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.819,
            0.611,
            0.853
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "denominator of the multiplier, 5, to get ${ \\frac { 3 } { 5 } } .$"
        },
        {
